WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.600
<i>A month has passed since that day.</i>

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.740
<i>μ hasn't been seen since.</i>

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.220
<i>Either the Musicians are 
quietly watching over things,</i>

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>or they're not making any obvious moves.</i>

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.570
<i>Meanwhile, our Go-Home Club...</i>

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.000
Oh, welcome back!

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.830
Sorry, it'll be ready in just a moment.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.450
Ah, it'll fall apart!

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.980
This is high-quality tofu, you know!

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.280
I'm beat.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.710
<i>It's now late spring, and the music prep room 
has become the Go-Home Club room, and...</i>

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.630
You're a high schooler, aren't you?

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.640
This is a façade.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.610
<i>...we've decided to share a hot pot.</i>

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:28.000
Work sure is hard.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.500
You look quite tired, Sempai.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.280
I never knew it was this 
harsh dealing with customers.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.920
I think I picked the wrong job.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.220
I can't believe you're working at 
an accessory shop, Shogo-sempai.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.240
Are you actually doing your job?

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.260
Of course.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.690
I have a full grasp of the 
products featured in the store,

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.450
and I help customers find—

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.930
Excuse me. How much is this?

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:53.550
Uh, huh? The price tag...

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.430
Where's the price tag?

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.040
Oh, here.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.650
No, that's not it.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.010
I handle the register smoothly, too.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.180
W-Will that be for yourself 
or a present for another?

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.370
A present.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.290
Th-Then I'll get you our 
gift bag as well.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.440
H-Huh?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.680
Where...

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.620
Bag, bag...

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.300
Hey, you still looking?! 
There's a line forming behind me!

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.710
I'm sorry!

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.060
The owner also has a lot of faith in me,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.510
but it's also a pain when 
they ask too much of me.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.520
I plan to quit soon.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.050
So well, I've been so busy it makes me dizzy.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.900
Is that true?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.520
Well, we're able to take it this easy only

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.240
because the Musicians are 
keeping a low profile.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.230
Oh, it's from Naruko-sempai.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.790
She says, "Shopping Squad B, now returning."

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.750
Is there anything extra we should ask for?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.960
We're good. Tell them to hurry back.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.230
Were you able to find it?

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.800
Oh, if you're talking about that...

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.510
Huh?

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.150
We're out of gas! And it was almost ready!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.240
Jeez!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.740
I will be the one to protect this world!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.750
Let's go, Rescue Dash!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:37.180
Argh, jeez! How long is this 
construction going to take?!

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:42.460
The repairs are handled by NPCs, 
so who knows how long it'll be?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.200
μ, hurry up and wake up.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.260
If you don't, I...

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.690
We...

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.120
This is all due to those Rogues.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.380
Damn annoyances.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.400
How did you get that scar?!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.860
I had a fight with someone I hate.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.440
That's all.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.960
IkeP...

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.170
That bastard...

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.120
Next time I'll get justice!

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.570
Hurry, hurry!

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:19.250
Everyone's waiting and looking 
forward to eating the Aria hot pot!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.480
Hurry up!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.730
"Aria hot pot"?

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.300
Why are you so worked up about this?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.800
Listen, when everyone 
gathers around a hot pot—

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:29.550
Hey.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.050
Will this do?

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.400
Way to go, Izurucchi!

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.560
Now let's get the hot pot started!

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.940
"Izurucchi"?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.100
Rescue Arm!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.000
Thank you, young man.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.950
Don't worry about it!

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:55.290
Ta-dah! For now, the first round's done!

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.410
Here, here! Eat up!

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.530
Go on! Go on! Eat lots!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.840
Well, time to eat.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.580
Thanks for the food!

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.080
Thanks for the food.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:11.300
It's good.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.210
It's delicious.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.010
Yeah.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.480
Hot pots really taste good when 
you eat with your friends, huh?

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:26.820
Man, adding these chicken meatballs really 
brings the best out of the hot pot!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.620
Very nice, Izuru!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.410
Another one!

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.250
You don't have to rush.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.120
There's still plenty more left.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.080
Lately I've just been so happy eating.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.290
Don't you mean you're having fun?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:43.850
Yes!

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.470
Ah! You're already eating!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.050
You could've waited a little bit longer!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.350
No!

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.890
This daikon isn't ready to eat yet!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.860
Eat the shiitake—the shiitake mushrooms!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.480
I-I don't need the shiitake mushrooms.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.730
And carrots, too!

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.400
I don't need carrots, either.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.480
You're not a child anymore.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.360
Though it shames me, Morita Naruko and 
Mizuguchi Marie have now returned!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.070
Pardon us.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.430
You're late, Naruko-sempai!

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.160
Well, sorry about that.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.680
Mizuguchi-san, you should 
come hang around more often.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.290
Or do you not like it here 
when the President's out?

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:23.370
Huh?

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.280
That's not true.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.320
I've just been busy lately.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:29.970
Now, then...

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:35.430
Today we've brought an incredible 
addition from Marie-chan!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.180
Oh!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.710
It's not that big a deal.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:45.040
I just wanted to have some with everyone 
when I heard we were having a hot pot.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.650
Don't be so modest!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.450
I-It looks delicious.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.030
<i>D-Damn...</i>

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.500
What should we do with this meat?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.320
The hot pot's full.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.870
Kotono, secure space!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:06.840
Roger!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.960
Thanks, Minezawa-kun!

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.010
We're leaving it up to you!

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.550
The fate of the world rests on my shoulders.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.060
There are more important things than meat!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.580
I changed out the gas.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.480
Thanks, Mizuguchi-san.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.700
Hey, can we eat that meat soon?

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.130
No! We eat after photos!

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.330
What?!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:45.750
Do you have any idea how much buzz 
that photos of expensive meat like this will get?!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.660
It's already getting responses!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.870
Oh, even more!

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.740
Everyone really is looking at me.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.750
That's enough now, right?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:58.180
If it boils too long, 
the meat will get tough.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.970
What, this is so good!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.080
It's a perfect accompaniment.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.280
Y-You idiot!

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.810
Do you have any idea what the value of a pic 
of a hot pot with expensive meat is?!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.940
Kotaro-sempai...

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.080
Stop!

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.290
Now, now, just leave him alone.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:29.750
Rescue! Oh, uh... Scoop!

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.130
Thank you, Rescue Man.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:36.220
No, this was nothing! Nothing at all!

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.390
Good, it's done!

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.720
Meat!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.970
<b>I'm still open for a ton of Rescues!!
Rescue Man</b>

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.970
<b>Rescue Man, help!!
I bought too many things from the 
special sale at the supermarket,
and now I can't carry it all. At this rate, 
I'll have to make several trips home.
It'd be a big help if you could help me. 
Mamannu</b>

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.770
Let's go, Rescue Dash!

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.730
This meat is so good.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.190
Well, I should be leaving.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.550
Thank you so much for the meat!

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.920
Come again!

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.120
Lately, Marie-chan's been 
coming to hang out often.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.880
Well, the President's not around today.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.250
Huh? Are those things related somehow?

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.170
Marie-sempai is coming 
here to see the President!

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:19.210
I think she shows shows up most 
often when the President's around.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.890
In other words...

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.810
Man, Sempai, you're dense!

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.030
Well, who cares if that's her reason?

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:32.480
Girls all love tales of sweet, 
stimulating romance.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.990
After all, we're made of sugar, 
spice, and everything nice.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.160
Oh, Rescue Man.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:48.810
Oh, he's busy, busy.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:55.840
Leaving him aside for now, 
has there been any new information?

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.120
Oh, that reminds me, 
before I went shopping...

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.740
H-Hey, Suzuna, what are you doing?

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.690
Huh? You didn't want udon in it?

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.350
That udon was for the end!

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.420
Huh? But my family always 
added it as a main ingredient.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.730
You don't?

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.540
The final... Aria udon...

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:18.030
Any meat still left—

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.650
You're at the end already?!

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:20.760
Damn!

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.200
Oh, Kotaro-kun, don't cry!

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.200
There are some fish balls left.
Here, udon too.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.830
<b>Uwaaah~! My cat ran off somewhere~ 
Help me, Rescue Man~!!
Emibbe</b>

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.830
<b>I'm still Rescuing!
Rescue Man</b>

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.830
<b>The ditch in front of my house is clogged,
 and water is flooding from it! It's really bad. Help me!
Thunder Man</b>

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.420
No rest for heroes of justice...

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.790
You idiots!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.100
Ah, Kotaro-sempai!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.960
It's good.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.010
<b>When you're in a desperate situation, 
it's all the more important to keep smiling.</b>

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:07.030
Where am I?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.590
The edge of the world? That's not it.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.440
I have a clear awareness of myself.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:23.400
So...

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:24.250
I figured it was you, μ.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.920
How is μ?

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:32.600
She's all right.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.870
It'll be soon. Don't worry.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.840
μ's consciousness is gradually awakening.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:44.460
Thanks to the power of her subconscious 
desire to protect us Musicians.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.740
Most likely, she'll wake up tonight.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.390
Gather everyone.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.220
Including the Musicians who aren't here.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.160
I've constantly been thinking.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:01.020
About what?

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.190
I want to make everyone happy.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.260
Yet the other day, I hurt you and the others.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:12.970
But everyone was going crazy at 
each other, so I lost control, as well.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:17.370
I couldn't understand myself anymore.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:19.800
Hey, Ritsu?

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.590
What should I do?

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:24.630
Why are you asking me?

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.900
Because you're you.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.820
That's not an answer.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.510
What can I do to make everyone happy?

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:37.160
What can I do to make you happy, too?

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:40.020
That's a difficult problem.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:49.820
Filling in whatever is missing 
doesn't always lead to happiness.

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:54.200
Well, the happiness one feels 
when obtaining something

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.660
shouldn't be denied, but...

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.620
It's so complicated that I don't understand.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.050
There are some people who derive 
joy from the suffering of others.

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:06.170
In that case, the unhappiness of one person

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:10.520
becomes happiness for someone else,
 creating an antinomy, right?

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.860
Hmm?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:17.000
It means that happiness 
differs for each individual.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.040
I don't really get that, either.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.300
Happiness is happiness, right?

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:23.880
How can it be different?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:27.680
People are happy when they have 
lots of delicious sweets, right?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:31.280
People are happy when they can wear 
as many cute outfits as they like.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.700
Also... Also, it's best when 
they all look really nice!

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.380
As I said...

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:39.910
Happiness is a way of thinking.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:41.120
Huh?

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:43.390
Ritsu?

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:47.710
N-No, real happiness is...

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.080
As I've told you before,

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:55.390
you should give yourself a bit more credit.

00:15:56.230 --> 00:16:00.480
...what you feel when you're fulfilled.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.190
You aren't happy when you 
obtain the things you want?

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.190
I...

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:14.810
So if your cherished pet dies, 
then I'll make an even cuter one for you.

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:19.040
If you have a mother you hate, 
I'll produce a new mother for you.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:19.610
See?

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:22.660
If I do that, then everyone 
can be happy, right?

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:25.750
μ...

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.830
Really?

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.090
What about your other options?

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:32.640
I don't have anything.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:34.390
I'm not like everyone else.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:40.020
There isn't a single person in this world 
who doesn't have some worry or problem.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:44.660
I've been listening to everyone's voices.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.570
The voices of their hearts,

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.980
crying out, "It hurts," "I'm in pain,"
 and "I want to be happy."

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:54.080
To put it another way, 
unhappiness is also just a belief.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:57.390
Pessimists don't even notice 
their own happiness.

00:16:57.390 --> 00:17:01.200
Yet the world is filled with plenty 
of small bits of happiness.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:04.540
That's something only the haves can say.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:08.410
You can forget about everything unpleasant.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:14.650
Everyone can be happy here in Mobius, 
where troubles, suffering, and pain don't exist.

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:17.560
A world that grants happiness...

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.100
Yes, that's right!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.310
This place is meant to make everyone happy!

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.570
So anything can be granted in Mobius.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.160
In other words, your happiness is—

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.940
Ritsu? What's wrong?

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:37.470
That's right.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.390
μ, you...

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.470
I...

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.500
Don't worry.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:48.170
I'll create your happiness for you, Ritsu.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.250
No.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.350
That's not right, μ.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:55.720
Listen to me.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.880
The things you want,

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.850
the wishes you want granted,

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.370
the people you want to see,

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.120
the emotions you want fulfilled,

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.710
the dreams you want to experience,

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.500
the way you want to look...

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.440
Don't worry.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.320
I'll grant any wish you have.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.660
With my song!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.980
Wait! I—

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.500
μ...

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.560
Oh, good morning.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.440
Good morning, μ.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:55.280
You've been sleeping so long 
that we were all getting worried.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:58.060
Yeah, I'm fine now.

00:18:58.060 --> 00:18:59.740
What's the matter?

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.110
In my dream...

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:07.200
I realized I need to work much, much harder.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.500
μ?

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.800
I'm sorry.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.080
I hurt all of you, didn't I?

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.510
It's fine.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:18.720
As long as you're around, 
we can all be happy again.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.830
That's right.

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:24.510
I'm sure Ritsu and the others 
just don't have enough happiness.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.930
That's why they're thinking about leaving.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:30.610
Yes, μ, exactly so.

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.390
So...

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:36.150
Why don't you let us all 
hear you sing some more?

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:37.580
Yeah!

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:42.120
The Musicians are gathering 
together again tonight.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.650
We should let them see that you're well.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.700
Okay.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.210
Huh?

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.020
What is this?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.850
Jeez, President, you're late!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.720
We've been waiting for you!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.930
Hmm? Did you stop somewhere on the way?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.350
Yeah, a bit.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:18.010
But the hot pot's over now.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:20.820
Mifue-chan ate a lot, didn't she?

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:20.820
Huh?!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.690
Hey, it wasn't just me, right?!

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:30.330
Ah, and here it was an Aria hot pot 
specially made by Aria, too.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.560
Ritsu, what's wrong?

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:37.980
Is it really over?

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.320
Huh?

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:43.010
It might look as though all the 
ingredients are gone at first glance,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.700
but unless the hot pot says it's over,

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:51.740
then I'm sure there are 
still possibilities left.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:55.650
We've got trouble!

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:57.870
Oh, it's Rescue Man.

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.370
N-No!

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:01.860
I'm not that hero of justice!

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:06.560
Saving people here in Mobius where people 
in need of rescue are prepared for you

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.990
is just self-satisfaction, Sempai.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.020
Shut up!

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:13.160
This is a matter of my heart!

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.150
More importantly, what's wrong?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.620
You're in a panic.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:19.140
I heard a scream from over there!

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:21.000
So stop eating that stuff, and let's hurry!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:25.180
Hey! Don't call my Aria special 
rice gruel "that stuff"!

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.180
What do you mean, "Aria special 
rice gruel," pipsqueak?!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.000
Could you save the comedy routine 
for later, Kotaro-sempai?

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:35.600
Huh? You're pretty cheeky 
for a newbie, Kensuke!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.320
I think it's probably what you told us about.

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:44.170
Then...

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.530
See? I told you to trust me.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.300
Then we're certain?

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:55.980
Go-Home Club, it's time to take action.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:32.010
We need to make Caligula more like **** 5

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Your life shouldn't be built from someone else's blueprint. 
No matter how unskilled you may be, you should draw it yourself.</b>

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.200
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:37.660
Your life shouldn't be built 
from someone else's blueprint.

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.980
No matter how unskilled you may be,
 you should draw it yourself.
